// EonlineBazar — PostgreSQL (Neon) schema — Stage 1 DESIGN ARTIFACT
// ============================================================================
// NOT ACTIVE. Nothing in the running system reads this file. The live system
// is MongoDB + Mongoose (backend/src/models/*.js) and stays authoritative
// until Stage 4 read cutover completes. See DATABASE_MIGRATION_AUDIT.md.
//
// Conventions (agreed in Stage 1 review):
//   * Field names are camelCase, identical to the Mongoose paths, so this file
//     can be diffed field-by-field against backend/src/models/*.js.
//     Table names are snake_case plural via @@map.
//   * Primary keys are String @id @default(uuid()) — MongoDB ObjectIds are
//     already string-like, which keeps the Stage 3 backfill a straight copy.
//   * `legacyId` holds the original MongoDB _id. It is the join key for the
//     Stage 3 backfill and makes re-running the backfill idempotent.
//   * Every currency column is @db.Decimal(12, 2). Percentages and rates are
//     @db.Decimal(5, 2) — they are not money and must not share the scale.
//   * onDelete is chosen per relation. Cascade is used ONLY for rows that are
//     owned by their parent (an Order's items, a User's addresses). Anything
//     cross-aggregate is SetNull or Restrict so that deleting a Category,
//     Supplier or Product can never destroy financial history.
// ============================================================================

// Prisma 7 note: the connection URL is NOT declared here. Since v7 the
// `url` / `directUrl` / `shadowDatabaseUrl` datasource properties are removed
// from the schema and live in `prisma.config.js` at the repo root, which reads
// DATABASE_URL from the repo-root .env.
//
// Generator: `prisma-client` — the current, non-deprecated generator.
// `prisma-client-js` is deliberately NOT used; Prisma has marked it deprecated
// and slated for removal, and this project picks forward-looking tooling now
// rather than migrating twice.
//
// `prisma-client` emits TypeScript only. In 7.10.0 there is no option that
// writes plain .js: `generatedFileExtension` accepts only "ts" | "mts" | "cts"
// (passing "js" is warned about and merely renames files whose contents are
// still TypeScript), and `moduleFormat` controls only whether __dirname or
// import.meta.url is used — not the emitted import/export syntax.
//
// `generatedFileExtension = "mts"` is what makes that output directly usable
// from this plain-CommonJS backend with no build step and no new dependency.
// Node runs .mts by stripping type annotations natively (unflagged since
// 22.18.0 / 23.6.0) and require() loads fully-synchronous ESM (unflagged since
// 20.19.0 / 22.12.0), so an ordinary .js file can do:
//
//   const { PrismaClient } = require('../../generated/prisma/client.mts');
//
// `moduleFormat = "esm"` must stay explicit: package.json is "type":
// "commonjs", so inference would pick cjs and emit __dirname, which does not
// exist in a .mts module. Requires Node >= 22.18.0 (running 24.16.0).
// An explicit `output` is mandatory — Prisma 7 no longer generates into
// node_modules. See DATABASE_MIGRATION_AUDIT.md, Stage 2 Step 1b.
generator client {
  provider               = "prisma-client"
  output                 = "../generated/prisma"
  runtime                = "nodejs"
  moduleFormat           = "esm"
  generatedFileExtension = "mts"
  importFileExtension    = "mts"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

